                  "before": "cff-version: 1.2.0\ntitle: Collaborative Human-Agent Protocol (CHAP)\nmessage: >-\n  If you use CHAP in academic or technical work, please cite the technical\n  report rather than this repository.\ntype: software\nauthors:\n  - given-names: Arsalan\n    family-names: Shahid\n    email: arsalan.shahid@brightbeam.com\n    affiliation: Brightbeam AI\n  - given-names: Gordon\n    family-names: Suttie\n    affiliation: Brightbeam AI\n  - given-names: Philip\n    family-names: Black\n    affiliation: Brightbeam AI\nrepository-code: https://github.com/BrightbeamAI/chap\nurl: https://github.com/BrightbeamAI/chap\nabstract: >-\n  An open protocol for recording human decisions over AI agent work.\n  Approvals, edits, overrides and escalations become queryable records in\n  one log per workspace, which can be signed and hash-chained. CHAP has a\n  small Core over JSON-RPC 2.0 and optional profiles, with two reference\n  implementations and MCP and A2A transports.\nkeywords:\n  - human-in-the-loop\n  - ai-agents\n  - audit\n  - provenance\n  - protocol\n  - model-context-protocol\n  - governance\nlicense:\n  - Apache-2.0\n  - CC-BY-4.0\nversion: 0.3.2\ndate-released: '2026-10-08'\npreferred-citation:\n  type: report\n  title: >-\n    Collaborative Human-Agent Protocol (CHAP): An open protocol for auditable,\n    structured multi-human and multi-agent collaboration\n  authors:\n    - given-names: Arsalan\n      family-names: Shahid\n      affiliation: Brightbeam AI\n    - given-names: Gordon\n      family-names: Suttie\n      affiliation: Brightbeam AI\n    - given-names: Philip\n      family-names: Black\n      affiliation: Brightbeam AI\n  institution:\n    name: Brightbeam AI\n  year: 2026\n  number: arXiv:2606.09751\n  url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09751\n  identifiers:\n    - type: other\n      value: arXiv:2606.09751\n      description: arXiv preprint identifier\n",
