          "context": "## What was asked\n\nTidy up after 0.3.2 and release 0.3.3: the review `deadline` line from\n#184, the ROADMAP row on failed writes, example 06's wording, CI on Node 24,\nand a release that carries the two changes merged since 0.3.2 (#186, #187).\n\n## What changed, and why\n\n- **Docs.** `profiles/review.md` says a review's `deadline` is recorded and\n  has no effect in this version of the profile, and `-32013` stays reserved\n  (closes #184). The ROADMAP gap row said the Python coordinator ignores a\n  failed write; since 0.3.2 both coordinators report it. Example 06 loses\n  its \"rather than\" opening and its slogan-like closing list, and says when\n  a lapse is recorded: when the deployment's lapse check runs.\n- **CI.** checkout, setup-node and setup-python move to v7, which run on\n  Node 24, so the deprecation warning on every job goes. The TypeScript and\n  template matrices add Node 24. Node 20 stays while the packages declare\n  `node >= 20`. Jobs that ran on Node 20 alone run on 24, and so does the\n  conformance Action by default.\n- **A TypeScript fix.** With a store that has only `save`, a workspace that\n  could not be serialised was skipped without a word. It is now reported\n  like any other failed write. The independent review found it.\n- **chap-analytics 0.2.4 and release 0.3.3.** Versions, pins, the lock file\n  and both changelogs. CITATION.cff gets this release's date, which had\n  stayed at 0.3.0's, and SECURITY.md stops naming 0.3.0 as the latest\n  release.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- TypeScript: build, typecheck and every package's tests, with SQLite\n  required, on Node 22 and on Node 24.\n- Python 3.10: chap-coordinator, the five bridges, chap-analytics and the\n  starter.\n- The conformance harness against the Python and TypeScript reference\n  servers, and the differential fuzzer on 25 seeds: all agree.\n- The version, schema, catalogue, error-code, em-dash and link checks.\n- An independent review of the branch. Its findings are fixed in these\n  commits, and the new TypeScript test fails without the fix.\n\n## Look closely at\n\n- The CI commit: the action versions and the Node matrices.\n- The TypeScript fix in `persistSnapshot`, and its test.\n- The 0.3.3 changelog entry."
